  "title": "US Market Intell Morning Briefing",
  "type": "morning_briefing",
  "priority": "high",
  "published": "2026-05-15",
  "insights": [
   "JPM remains tactically bullish on US markets, citing resilient consumer-led macro, strong earnings, and renewed tech interest.",
   "Data Intel team issues a tactical bearish call on XLK, noting retail sentiment has not kept pace with the price rally to all-time highs.",
   "Semiconductors show high retail crowding (~100th percentile), while software positioning remains at lows, creating a potential short-squeeze setup in software.",
   "Trading desk reports significant outflows from EM (Taiwan, Korea) as retail-driven momentum in those regions fades.",
   "Middle East geopolitical tensions remain a primary risk, with JPM commodities desk in Dubai warning that a restart to military action is more likely than a diplomatic resolution.",
   "Retail sales growth in the post-COVID era has roughly doubled compared to the five years preceding COVID, supported by record consumer cash piles."
  ],
  "sector_views": [
   {
